All solutions are correct and efficient for the problem at hand. However, Solution B and Solution C are more concise and leverage Python's built-in string methods, which might make them slightly more readable and maintainable. Since both B and C use similar logic, they are the most consistent in terms of approach and reliability. Given the requirement to choose the most consistent solution, I will select one of these two. Between B and C, Solution C is slightly more consistent in its handling of the start index, making it a bit more straightforward to understand and less prone to off-by-one errors.</thought>
